    [44917,48958,"Banks","Archee","Archee is a courteous, gracious young adult with a gentle and genuine demeanour. Within our school community, Archee’s attendance at the Athletics and Swimming Carnivals has enriched those events and demonstrates the valuable contributions he can make and his capacity to support the collaborative team culture of Aranda House. Archee also competed in the Netball School Cup and participates in co-curricular Football. His involvement in the Peer Support Programme shows his concern for others and his emerging leadership potential. His treatment of the younger students modelled patience and enthusiasm. Archee is always punctual to Mentor time and demonstrates his pride in being a member of the school community by wearing his uniform appropriately. Archee’s achievements are already pleasing and form a strong foundation for further growth and development. "],
    [44917,49135,"Barbas","George","George is to be commended for his fine efforts this semester. He has laid himself a solid foundation on which to build for next semester and I encourage him to continue striving towards his goals. Within our school community George’s attendance at the Athletics and Swimming Carnivals has enriched those events and demonstrates the valuable contributions he can make and his capacity to support the collaborative team culture of Kogara House. George also enjoys a rich co-curricular life and has recently taken part in a prestigious Robotics competition, proceeding to represent Australia internationally. He is always kind and considerate, treating others with dignity and respect and is a strong role model for younger students. His involvement in the Student Host and Peer Support Programmes shows his concern for others and his emerging leadership potential. George always wears his uniform appropriately and has recently been awarded a Dean's award in recognition of his efforts."],
    [44917,11231,"Barber","Olivia","Olivia is a hardworking and punctual student who takes pride in her uniform and application to her studies. Within our school community, Olivia’s attendance at the Athletics, Cross Country and Swimming Carnivals has enriched those events and demonstrates the valuable contributions she can make and her capacity to support the collaborative team culture of Aranda House. Olivia was an active participant during the Peer Support Programme where she supported younger students during their camp experience endeavouring to instill self belief. She also worked enthusiastically with staff during the Try TIGS Day demonstrating solid leadership skills. Olivia’s consistent effort across all subject areas is testament to the positive attitude with which she approaches her work. "],
    [44917,45861,"Bigirindavyi","Esther","Esther is a friendly member of the Year 10 group. Within our school community, Esther’s attendance at the Swimming, Athletics and Cross Country Carnivals has enriched those events and demonstrates the valuable contributions she can make and her capacity to support the collaborative team culture of Wolgal House. She has a strong Christian faith and I rely on her regularly to lead our Year Meetings in prayer. This is much appreciated. Esther is also a talented performer and is currently rehearsing for the School Production ‘High School Musical’. Her role as an Arts Leader compliments her gifts and allowing her to genuinely model and demonstrate the importance of involvement in co-curricular activities. Esther is a valued member of our Year Group and I look forward to witnessing her future growth and maturity. "],
    [44917,48422,"Bodey","Katie","Katherine is a friendly and energetic student in our Year Group. Within our school community, Katherine’s attendance at the Swimming, Athletics and Cross Country Carnivals has enriched those events and demonstrates the valuable contributions she can make and her capacity to support the collaborative team culture of Aranda House. Her involvement in the Student Host and Outdoor Education Programmes shows her concern for others and her emerging leadership potential.  Katherine also took part in the Athletics Squad, Girls Fitness Programme, participates regularly as a musician in the Chapel Band and is a current participant in the Duke of Edinburgh Award. In addition to this, Katherine also qualified for participation in the CIS Girls Soccer competition. She always wears his uniform appropriately and interacts with others in a friendly, polite, respectful manner. Katherine has recently been awarded a Dean's award in recognition of her efforts. It is a privilege to have shared his journey so far and exciting to anticipate the opportunities and possibilities of the journey still to come."],
    [44917,60078,"Borbilas","Dean","Dean’s willingness to participate in the variety of co-curricular opportunities offered to students at The Illawarra Grammar School is impressive. The enthusiasm with which he approaches all aspects of school life is a positive influence on those around him. Dean has taken part in a number of sporting events and has been a fine ambassador for our School.  He was chosen to represent at the NASSA Football Gala day, AICES Under 16 Football team, AICES Open Football team, CIS Cup Soccer team and Under 16 Futsal team. These many sporting achievements demonstrate a commitment to hard work to both his regular training sessions and his ongoing school assessment tasks. Dean consistently wears his uniform with pride indicating his sense of belonging to the The Illawarra Grammar School community. His position as an Outdoor Education Leader has also allowed him to develop in managing people and his own sense of self. Dean has recently been awarded a Dean's award in recognition of his efforts. "],
    [44917,41244,"Budak","Koray","Koray is a kind and polite student. His willingness to participate in the variety of opportunities offered to students at The Illawarra Grammar School is impressive. Koray’s determination and fitness prowess is demonstrated through his commitment to participating in the Duke of Edinburgh Award and position as an Outdoor Education Leader. He conducted himself in an exemplary manner, modelling by example to the younger students in his care. Koray has also participated enthusiastically at the School Swimming, Athletics and Cross Country Carnivals and participated during the House ArtsFest competition in vital roles for the Dance section and Vocal Solo and House Song. Koray is a valued member of our Year Group."],
    [44917,63641,"Chancharoen","Boonsita (Jeny)","Boonsita has made a pleasing start to her time here at The Illawarra Grammar School. She has settled into academic work well and is enjoying the learning opportunities available to her. It is pleasing to see Boonsita becoming more involved in the wider life of the School. Her participation at the Cross Country and Athletics Carnivals is evidence of her engagement and willingness to build connections between her peers. I encourage her to continue striving to fulfil her potential and educational commitments."],
    [44917,11469,"Cooper","Jayson","Jayson is a friendly and amiable student. Pleasingly, there is a growth and maturity being made evident in my interactions with Jayson this semester. He is exhibiting a more conscientious attitude towards his studies and has been involved in the life of the school through House events such as the Swimming Carnival, Cross Country Carnival, and most recently, the Athletics Carnival.  I encourage Jayson to seek as many opportunities during the next two years to use his gifts and talents generously and apply these areas to school life. Also importantly, to value and recognise the positive and genuine elements of his personality and the role he plays within our Year 10 group. Jayson has recently been awarded a Dean's award in recognition of his efforts. "],
    [44917,48741,"Di Noro","Ilaria","Ilaria has shown a pleasing level of involvement in co-curricular activities as she continues to foster her holistic development. There is a level of growth and maturity being made evident in my interactions with Ilaria this semester. She is exhibiting a conscientious attitude towards her studies and has been involved in the life of the school through House events such as the Swimming Carnival, Cross Country Carnival and most recently, the Athletics Carnival. Her position as an Outdoor Education leader has also allowed her to grow in managing people and her own sense of self.  Ilaria’s involvement in ArtsFest was recognised as her artistic abilities were utilised. These are further complemented in her commitment to the Art From the Heart Programme. I look forward to witnessing Ilaria’s further development and growth throughout her senior years at The Illawarra Grammar School."],
    [44917,49225,"Do","Xavier","Xavier’s general contribution to the life of the school in both sporting and co-curricular activities has been excellent. The enthusiasm with which he approaches all aspects of school life is a positive influence on those around him.  Xavier has been able to balance his academic pursuits successfully with participation and success in many co-curricular and cultural activities. This indicates a high level of maturity and organisational skills. An example of this was his involvement in the Da Vinci Decathlon competition, achieving 4th in the regional area overall.  Xavier’s musical talents were also recognised by the music staff when Xavier was chosen to play a key role in the School Production. He also compliments his musical and artistic abilities with participation in the Duke of Edinburgh Award. Xavier’s servant-hearted attitude has been displayed during many instances this semester. He has volunteered to assist at the School Fete as well as acting as a Student Host for visiting schools during the Debating competition.  Xavier was also an active participant during the Peer Support Programme where he supported students from the younger year group during their camp experience, endeavouring to instil self-belief. Xavier has recently been awarded a Dean's award in recognition of his efforts which is a commendable achievement."],
    [44917,49544,"Dove","Maxi","Max is to be commended for his efforts this semester and I encourage him to continue striving towards his goals. Max has taken on the role as a Media leader and this appears to be an area in which he excels with his natural talent for creativity and musical, artistic abilities. I encourage Max to seek as many opportunities during the next two years to use his gifts and talents generously and apply these areas to school life. Max consistently wears his uniform with pride indicating his sense of belonging to the school community. He regularly attends Game On during Tuesday lunch times and continues to forge friendships and connections with his fellow Year 10 peers."],
