    [44917,43383,"Gyngell","Sally","Sally is a friendly member of the Year 10 group. Within our school community, Sally’s attendance at the Swimming, Athletics and Cross Country Carnivals has enriched those events and demonstrates the valuable contributions she can make and her capacity to support the collaborative team culture of Wolgal House. Sally’s impressive array of involvement includes participating in the HICES Debating and Mock Trial competitions, Senior Choir and Chapel Band and a performer in the School Production. This plethora of activities indicates not only her dedication and pursuit of excellence to her interests but also, generosity of her time, gifts and talents to our school. Sally also wears her uniform with pride representing her sense of belonging to the The Illawarra Grammar School community. I regularly rely on Sally to assist as a volunteer Student Host at different School functions and events. Her enthusiasm and good nature is much appreciated. "],
    [44917,46473,"Healey","James","James’ willingness to participate in the variety of co-curricular opportunities offered to students at The Illawarra Grammar School is impressive. The enthusiasm with which he approaches all aspects of school life is a positive influence on those around him.  James has taken part in several sporting events and has been a fine ambassador for our school. He was chosen to compete in the CIS Cup Soccer competition and also to represent the School at NASSA Cross Country. James further competed at the prestigious level of New South Wales CIS Swimming and took part in the New South Wales All Schools Triathlon teams event. He also represented the School in the Netball Schools Cup. James’ Determination and fitness prowess was further demonstrated during the ANZAC hike in the Blue Mountains. These many sporting achievements demonstrate a commitment to hard work to both his regular training sessions and his ongoing school assessment tasks. His position as an Outdoor Education Leader has allowed him to develop in managing people and his own sense of self. It has been wonderful to witness James’ journey of growth and enrichment and I look forward to sharing the challenges and opportunities of the years ahead."],
