    [44917,529,"Kiteley","Harrison","Harrison’s willingness to participate in the variety of co-curricular opportunities offered to students at The Illawarra Grammar School is impressive. The enthusiasm with which he approaches all aspects of school life is a positive influence on those around him. Harrison has taken part in several sporting events and has been a fine ambassador for our school.  He represented NASSA in the Tennis Gala day, Netball Schools Cup, Under 16 Futsal team, and CIS Cup Soccer team. He was also chosen to represent our school at the AICES Tennis competition, which was a fine achievement. Harrison is also a keen golfer and achieves at an exemplary level in this sport. His amiable personality and disposition endear him to both students and staff. I would always encourage Harrison to be more conscious of wearing his school uniform with pride. Harrison is aware of the upcoming commitments necessary for senior study and I am confident he will be willing to commit to these requirements.  Harrison has recently been awarded a Dean's award in recognition of his efforts. "],
    [44917,12752,"Koder","Lucy","Lucy’s willingness to participate in the variety of co-curricular opportunities offered to students at The Illawarra Grammar School is impressive. The enthusiasm with which she approaches all aspects of school life is a positive influence on those around her. Lucy’s school spirit is evident through her involvement in all House activities. This plethora of activities indicates not only her dedication and pursuit of excellence to her interests but also the generosity of her time, gifts and talents to our school. Her impressive array of involvement further includes competing in the Public Speaking and HICES Debating competitions, participation in the Mock Trial competition, a Year 10 participant in Community Problem Solving investigating the topic of Education for Lower Socio Economic Primary Students and competing in the Da Vinci Decathlon which scored 4th place in the region. Lucy’s endeavours to constantly seek and study new ideas was fulfilled during her foray into learning at The Notre Dame University. Not only does Lucy take part in these many worthwhile activities, she is also actively involved as a servant hearted leader undertaking the World Vision cause. It has been wonderful to witness Lucy’s journey of growth and enrichment and I look forward to sharing the challenges and opportunities of the years ahead. "],
