    [44917,49261,"Sams","Daisy","Daisy is a gentle, genial student with a thoughtful, introspective nature. Belying her quiet, reflective demeanour, though, is an inner strength and determination. With her increasing confidence to express herself more frequently, Daisy is evolving into an important voice and role model within our school. Daisy’s participation in the ArtsFest House Song shows her willingness to support the team culture of Coligan House, but it would be wonderful to see her becoming more actively involved in other school activities. Daisy’s involvement in the Reconciliation Walk illustrates her capacity to be a proud ambassador for her indigenous culture. Daisy is punctual to Mentor time each morning and demonstrates her pride in being a member of the school community by wearing her uniform appropriately. Daisy should now continue to foster her leadership potential by trusting in the strength and power of her own voice. It is a privilege to have shared her journey so far and exciting to anticipate the opportunities and possibilities of the journey still to come. "],
    [44917,45250,"Scott","Samuel","Samuel is a friendly and personable student in our Year Group. Within our school community, Samuel’s attendance at the Swimming, Athletics and Cross Country Carnivals has enriched those events and demonstrates the valuable contributions he can make and his capacity to support the collaborative team culture of Coligan House. His involvement in the Student Host and Peer Support Programmes shows his concern for others and his emerging leadership potential. He is often the first student to volunteer his time, gifts and talents for school events and functions. Samuel is a student upon whom I regularly rely."],
