    [44917,1055,"Wilson","Xia Lian","Xia Lian’s willingness to participate in the variety of co-curricular opportunities offered to students at The Illawarra Grammar School  is impressive. The enthusiasm with which she approaches all aspects of school life is a positive influence on those around her. Xia Lian has been involved in a plethora of activities which indicates not only her dedication and pursuit of excellence to her interests but also the generosity of her time, gifts and talents to our School. Her impressive array of involvement includes a role in the School Production, competing in the Public Speaking school competition, participating in the HICES Debating competition, participation in the Mock Trial competition, involvement in the TIGS Senior Choir and competing in the Da Vinci Decathlon which scored 4th place in the region. Not only does Xia Lian take part in these many worthwhile activities, she is also actively involved as a servant hearted leader taking on ownership of the Peer Reading groups for the Junior School and regularly volunteering to assist as a host at the Great Fete, a buddy for new students and assisting at the inauguration of our new principal Mrs Judi Nealy. Xia Lian has recently been awarded a Dean's award in recognition of her efforts. "],
